# Related Navigation

Offer a few links that help someone finish or understand the current task. Order them by need, label the group specifically and link only to places the person is allowed to open. It is not a second site map.

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation. They do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## When to use it

Use a small set after a device guide or beside a long article, for example a device manual beside a maintenance record. Do not rank links by an assumed popularity score.

## Structure and behaviour

Mark the group as navigation and give it a specific name such as “More about theme installation”. Use short destination titles. On narrow screens, put related links after the main content, in the same reading order. Say when a link leaves Home Assistant or the documentation, following [Write effective links](../../content/writing-guidelines/add-links.html).

## Home Assistant boundary

The theme does not infer household relationships, expose hidden dashboards or recommend external services. Do not copy government organisation, world-location or policy classifications into the household interface.

